          "create_time": 1789752232.092718,
          "update_time": 1789752237.325894,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Done. The patch below supersedes the earlier one (apply from the repo root with `git apply wilson-lines-20260918-claude.patch`); the tarball holds the same 14 files. Here is what the second session added, in the order of the continuation note's list.\n\n**1. The OS-positivity audit is settled at the level it can be.** DeWolfe–Freedman–Ooguri's eq. (4.30) is exactly the reflection through the defect, $P_6$, and they state it is a symmetry of the full bulk-plus-defect action, with $\\Phi\\to\\bar\\Phi$ — so $X_V$ even, $X_H$ **odd**, $A_6$ odd, defect fields inert. My reading of the source's Appendix B was right, and it is now their statement rather than mine. What remains of the positivity hypothesis is Osterwalder–Schrader positivity itself for a symmetry reflection, the standard assumption for any unitary QFT.\n\n**2. Endpoint conditions for the kets.** The common charge's Killing spinor $x\\cdot\\Gamma\\epsilon_c$ vanishes at the reference point, so there is no condition at the origin; at the outer end the local BPS condition reduces in one line to $J\\epsilon_c=-\\epsilon_c$, the same condition as the common charge and the chirality that (per the source's Appendix C) annihilates $q_1$ — identically at $+r$ and $-r$, which is what the even average needs. The last step is a reading of Appendix C, not a re-derivation.\n\n**3. First interaction correction, partly.** I inventoried the six first-order diagrams for the network kernel. The arc self-exchange is the source's constant. The new cross-arc exchange is computed: because $X_H$ is odd, the reflection-positive pairing path flips its scalar coupling at the origin, and that junction is a *scalar cusp* with one-loop anomalous dimension $\\gamma_J=g^2C_F/2\\pi^2=\\Gamma_{\\rm cusp}(\\phi=0,\\theta=\\pi)$ — a known observable rather than a feature of this construction. Its finite part $f(u,\\sigma)$ is tabulated (grid-converged to $10^{-4}$ for $u\\le2$); its large-$u$ slope is $-1$, exactly what conformal covariance demands from $\\gamma_J$, and it differs between the same-ray and opposite-ray halves. So this diagram alone does not preserve the even tower coefficient by coefficient; whether the full sum does, with shifted weight, depends on the two remaining diagrams.\n\n**A question for you about your own paper.** The source lists three $O(g^4)$ corrections to (58). A fourth candidate — exchange of the line's $X^H_3$ with the defect vertex $\\bar q\\,\\sigma^3(D_6X_H)\\,q$, which has $\\sigma^3_{11}=1$ and a nonvanishing pinned-derivative propagator off the defect — appears not to be among them. Either a symmetry kills it or the $1+4/\\pi^2$ changes. You can settle this faster than I can.\n\n**Housekeeping.** The check programme is now registered in `validation/endpoint_matter.py` (1350 cases replay identically, record refreshed with both models named), the exploratory table and the note are bound into the provenance record, all indexes, the CHANGELOG, the continuation note and `NEW_SESSION_PROMPT.md` are updated. Manuscript untouched at 0.8; the 17 September review's corrections remain unapplied and the notes have now outrun it by a day."
            ]
